-- title:
--   Normal forms of the quadratic and cubic mathfrakgl₃ Casimirs
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a ring carrying an algebra structure over $\mathbb{C}$, and let $e : \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \to \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \to A$ be a family of nine elements $e_{ij}$ satisfying, for all indices $i,j,k,l \in \{0,1,2\}$ without exception, the commutation relations of the elementary matrices of $\mathfrak{gl}_3$: $e_{ij}e_{kl} - e_{kl}e_{ij}$ equals $e_{il}$ if $j = k$ (and $0$ otherwise) minus $e_{kj}$ if $l = i$ (and $0$ otherwise). The conclusion is a conjunction of two identities in $A$, multiples being taken by natural numbers. First, the quadratic Casimir element satisfies $\sum_{i,j} e_{ij}e_{ji} = (e_{00}^2 + e_{11}^2 + e_{22}^2 - 2e_{00} + 2e_{22}) + \big(e_{01}(2e_{10}) + e_{02}(2e_{20}) + e_{12}(2e_{21})\big)$. Second, the cubic Casimir element satisfies $\sum_{i,j,k} e_{ij}(e_{jk}e_{ki}) = \big(e_{00}^3 + e_{11}^3 + e_{22}^3 - 2e_{00}^2 + e_{11}^2 + 4e_{22}^2 - (e_{00}e_{11} + e_{00}e_{22} + e_{11}e_{22}) - 2e_{00} - 2e_{11} + 4e_{22}\big) + \big(e_{01}\cdot 3(e_{00}e_{10} + e_{11}e_{10} + e_{12}e_{20}) + e_{02}\cdot 3(e_{00}e_{20} + e_{10}e_{21} + e_{20} + e_{22}e_{20}) + e_{12}\cdot 3(e_{11}e_{21} + 2e_{21} + e_{22}e_{21})\big)$. In each case the first bracket is a polynomial in the diagonal letters $e_{00}, e_{11}, e_{22}$ alone, and the second bracket lies in the right ideal generated by the strictly upper-triangular letters $e_{01}, e_{02}, e_{12}$, each of the displayed tail monomials being written with its upper-triangular letter on the left.
--
--   This is an explicit Harish-Chandra-type normal form for the degree-two and degree-three central elements of $U(\mathfrak{gl}_3)$: modulo the right ideal generated by the strictly upper-triangular generators, each Casimir element is congruent to a stated polynomial in the diagonal generators, with no $\rho$-shift performed and with the convention that the upper-triangular letter stands leftmost in every tail monomial. It is used in [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.casimir_eq_smul_of_deriv_archRealLift3_mul_eq`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.casimir_eq_smul_of_deriv_archRealLift3_mul_eq), where the Casimir elements are evaluated on a vector annihilated by the raising operators.
